<article class="env-lemma" id="06CS">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06CS">Lemma <span data-tag="06CS">76.19.11</span>.</a> The property $\mathcal{P}(f) =$“$f$ is formally smooth” is fpqc local on the base. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $f : X \to Y$ be a morphism of algebraic spaces over a scheme $S$. Choose an index set $I$ and diagrams 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ U_ i \ar[d] \ar[r]_{\psi _ i} &  V_ i \ar[d] \\  X \ar[r]^ f &  Y }  \]
</div>
    <p>
       with étale vertical arrows and $U_ i$, $V_ i$ affine schemes. Moreover, assume that $\coprod U_ i \to X$ and $\coprod V_ i \to Y$ are surjective, see Properties of Spaces, Lemma <a href="/tag/03FX" data-tag="03FX">66.6.1</a>. By Lemma <a href="/tag/061K" data-tag="061K">76.19.10</a> we see that $f$ is formally smooth if and only if each of the morphisms $\psi _ i$ are formally smooth. Hence we reduce to the case of a morphism of affine schemes. In this case the result follows from Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/06CM" data-tag="06CM">10.138.16</a>. Some details omitted. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>